    "narrative": "For July 2, 2026, the offensive core for LawDog centers around **Jonathan Aranda**, whose 68.94 score makes him our premier start. Facing Kolek, **Aranda** benefits from a high-leverage #2 lineup spot, a positive wind factor, and a favorable xwOBA environment that pushes his efficiency well above the base projection. **Bryson Stott** (63.08) and **Masyn Winn** (62.77) follow closely as strong plays; **Winn** is specifically bolstered by a massive +19% SP skill boost against Waldrep\u2019s inflated 7.82 xERA. While **Gavin Sheets** (61.22) provides a solid floor, his start is contingent on confirming the #2 spot against the formidable Roki Sasaki; if **Sheets** is dropped in the order, his efficiency score will likely dip below our 60-point \"Strong\" threshold.\n\n**Cal Raleigh** (56.58) sits as our most marginal start, falling just short of the 60-point mark due to the dynamic platoon penalty associated with facing Ure\u00f1a. While **Raleigh** remains in the lineup to maximize our power upside, he is the primary candidate to be managed if we need to preserve game caps later in the week. Given the rest of the bench\u2014including stalwarts like **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez**, **Lawrence Butler**, **Geraldo Perdomo**, and **Yainer Diaz**\u2014are either currently on the IL or facing an off-day, our tactical flexibility is limited today. We are essentially riding our primary options to exploit the soft matchup against Waldrep while keeping a watchful eye on potential lineup shifts for **Gavin Sheets**. No other bench assets, such as **Tyler Freeman**, **Will Smith**, **Taylor Ward**, **Matt Chapman**, **Daulton Varsho**, **Luis Arraez**, **Dylan Beavers**, **Jeremiah Jackson**, **Brendan Donovan**, **Jung Hoo Lee**, **Gleyber Torres**, **Ryan Waldschmidt**, or **Drew Gilbert**, were in a position to challenge the starters for a spot due to schedule constraints or current health status.",
